  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/acb15856-5763-459b-84d4-d44d68f02551-image.png\" style=\"width: 317px; height: 300px;\" /></p><p>Solvent polarity has been related to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> value of nitrocompounds.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mg</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>-nitrophenol and picric acid have different <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> value on silica gel plate</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Preparative TLC is best to separate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mg</mi></math> of para nitrophenol and picric acid</p></blockquote>",
